{
  "0": "Sequence modeling: set the causal context cap to max(1, floor(0.9 * current_maxlen)), preserving chronological order and all shorter histories. This milder truncation may remove stale interactions while retaining useful context lost by the previously tested 0.75 multiplier. Apply identically during training and prediction across all four datasets; preserve embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer.",
  "1": "Training strategy: multiply the incumbent learning rate by 0.7, leaving optimizer type, batch size, dropout, weight decay and scheduler rules unchanged. Smaller updates may reduce the observed validation oscillation and improve generalization, particularly for Electronics. Preserve the architecture, loss, sampling, seed 42, 200-epoch cap and existing validation checkpoint selection across all four datasets.",
  "2": "Network architecture: apply layer normalization separately to the GRU reset, update and candidate gate preactivations, retaining existing hidden width, recurrent depth and gate equations otherwise. Stabilizing gate scales may prevent saturation and improve recurrent optimization without widening or deepening the model. Preserve embeddings, history selection, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer; update the predictor writer to reconstruct this single trained network per dataset.",
  "3": "Learning objective: replace the prediction loss with mean softplus(0.2 + negative_score - positive_score), using exactly the existing sampled negatives and masking. A modest pairwise margin may improve separation near the HR@10 ranking boundary without emphasizing already easy negatives. Preserve features, embeddings, GRU topology, scoring, readout, optimizer, sampling and training schedule; train one model per dataset."
